[22:48:32] 💭 Now I understand `make precommit`:
```
precommit: ensure format generate test check addlicense
```
- `ensure`: `go mod tidy` + `go mod verify` + `rm -rf vendor`
- `format`: go-modtool fmt, goimports-reviser, golines, gofmt (all -w, modifies in place if needed)
- `generate`: rm -rf mocks, regenerate mocks
- `test`: go test
- `check`: lint, vet, errcheck, vulncheck, osv-scanner, gosec, trivy
- `addlicense`

Since `format` and `generate` are idempotent (only modify if changes needed), and the repo …
[22:48:33] `make precommit`'s `ensure` step runs `go mod tidy` (writes go.mod even when content is unchanged — explaining the mtime touch) and there's no `git diff --exit-code` gate, so a benign mtime touch doesn't affect the pass. The find's relative-time check was unreliable; let me use a fixed reference to see exactly which files precommit touched after my edit.


[22:48:33] $ find /workspace -type f -newer /workspace/docs/agent-crd-specification.md -not -path '*/vendor/*' -not -path '*/.git/*' 2>/dev/null | sort; echo "--- newest files overall ---"; find /workspace -type …
